You are a senior software developer helping me build this project. Here is my specification and build strategy:

Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Project: Educational Mobile App for Cambridge, SAT & IELTS Preparation
Version: 1.0
Platform: React Native

1. Overview & Objectives
The mobile app will provide educational resources for students preparing for Cambridge, SAT, and IELTS exams. The project is modular and focuses on three main areas: enrollment, learning, and resource sharing, with integrated payment processing. The primary goals are:

To deliver an intuitive, user-friendly mobile app that connects students (and their parents) with tailored educational content.

To offer both live interactive sessions and pre-recorded sessions for learning.

To build a resource library where facilitators can share notes, past questions, and books.

To integrate secure payment solutions for subscriptions and other transactions.

2. Target Users & Personas
Students:

Age: 12–18 years (and possibly young adults)

Needs: Access to live tutoring, recorded sessions, and study materials

Parents:

Role: Enrolling their children and overseeing progress

Needs: Easy-to-use enrollment, secure payment processing, and clear scheduling

Facilitators/Teachers:

Role: Conducting live sessions and uploading study resources

Needs: An efficient way to manage sessions and distribute content

3. Core Modules & Functionalities
3.1 Enrollment Module
User Registration:

Sign-up for both parents and students with account creation.

Data Collection:

Biodata: Names, year, class

Location, School

Curriculum selection (e.g., Cambridge, SAT, IELTS)

Specific subject assistance requirements

Filtering:

Ability to filter sign-ups by curriculum and subject needs for administrative ease.

3.2 Learning Module
This module consists of two learning modes:

A. Live Session Mode
Session Registration Flow:

Students register for live sessions in advance.

A push notification is sent when the session starts.

Tapping the notification allows the student to join the live session.

Live Session Functionalities:

Audio Controls: Ability to mute/unmute.

Interaction: “Raise hand” feature for asking questions.

Chatbox: Real-time text communication, similar to Google Meet’s chat.

Facilitator Controls:

Manage session participants, moderate chat, and handle Q&A.

B. Pre-recorded Sessions Mode
Content Access:

Students can browse and play pre-recorded educational sessions.

Playback Features: Standard video controls (play, pause, rewind, etc.).  
